                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>richTextValue</name>
                    <value>&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:107%&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;Dear IACMI Consortium Members,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#212121&quot;&gt;We are excited to announce the return of IACMI Consortium Elections for 2021!&amp;nbsp; This year, IACMI Consortium Members are being asked to nominate representatives to serve on the IACMI Consortium Council.&amp;nbsp; The Council oversees the activities of the IACMI Consortium and helps select IACMI projects and programs. As a Consortium Member, IACMI values your leadership within our community, and you may nominate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt; yourself or another IACMI member representative&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#212121&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;to serve on behalf of the [&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;Small/Medium Enterprise Companies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#212121&quot;&gt;/Large Entity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt; Companies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#212121&quot;&gt;/State, National Laboratory, or Academic Organization].&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;There will be 2 SME representatives elected, and 1 each from the Large Entity and State, National Laboratory or Academic Organization members.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#212121&quot;&gt;Please enter your nominations by visiting&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#0563c1&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/2019large-nominations&quot; style=&quot;color:blue; text-decoration:underline&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:#80ff80&quot;&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:#80ff80&quot;&gt;WEBSITE FOR SPECIFIC CLASS ELECTION(S)]&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#212121&quot;&gt;by &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;Friday&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#212121&quot;&gt;, January 2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;9&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#212121&quot;&gt;, 2021 at 5PM EST.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt; &lt;u&gt;All nominees must be from entities that have paid their 2021 membership fees or have scheduled to pay them no later than February 28, 2021&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#212121&quot;&gt;Once we have gathered all the nominees and placed them on the appropriate&amp;nbsp;election&amp;nbsp;page, you will be sent a link on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;Tuesday&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#212121&quot;&gt;, February &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#212121&quot;&gt;, 2021, to cast your final votes for&amp;nbsp;the Council. Please note that only one individual per organization is permitted to vote.&amp;nbsp; Council&amp;nbsp;election&amp;nbsp;winners will be notified as soon as possible after February 12, 2021, pending no additional runoff is needed to break a tie vote, and all IACMI members will be notified of the new board representatives on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:yellow&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#212121&quot;&gt;​or&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#212121&quot;&gt;by February &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;28&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#212121&quot;&gt;, 2021, at the latest.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#212121&quot;&gt;The&amp;nbsp;IACMI staff appreciates your leadership and engagement within our IACMI community.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;For more information regarding the&amp;nbsp;elections please visit [&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:#80ff80&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#212121&quot;&gt;WEBPAGE for Election Information]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#212121&quot;&gt;.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;If there are any questions or comments not answered by the aforementioned page, please feel free to email Zack R. Gardner (&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:zgardner@iacmi.org&quot; style=&quot;color:blue; text-decoration:underline&quot;&gt;zgardner@iacmi.org&lt;/a&gt;).&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#212121&quot;&gt;The IACMI Consortium Council Generally:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background:white&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#212121&quot;&gt;The IACMI Consortium Council is vested with the authority to manage the activities and affairs of the IACMI Consortium. The Council, working with the CCS BOD of Directors and IACMI Staff, approves strategic plans, annual budgets, technical plans, projects, and IACMI management practices. The Council examines the operational status of ongoing IACMI projects including indicators such as progress versus milestones and schedules, resource capacity, and resource availability. The Council reviews the pipeline of proposed new projects and other IACMI opportunities. These reviews result in tactical decisions and resource adjustments to optimize the flow of the overall IACMI project portfolio.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:black&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;Thank you,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&amp;nbsp;</value>
